---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="tbt — Cognitive Acceleration for Infants" description="AI-powered early learning system combining Doman, Shichida, and Artificial Synesthesia">
  <article class="case-study">
    <header class="case-header">
      <div class="case-meta">
        <span class="case-tenets">
          <a href="/ai">AI</a>
          <a href="/clarity">Clarity</a>
          <a href="/story">Story</a>
        </span>
        <span class="case-industry">
          <a href="/industries/education">Education</a>
        </span>
      </div>
      <h1>tbt</h1>
      <p class="case-tagline">Cognitive Acceleration for Infants</p>
    </header>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">The Research</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        What if the first three years of life aren't for passive play — but represent the brain's 
        most powerful learning window?
      </p>
      <p>
        The Glenn Doman Method and Makoto Shichida's right-brain training have shown for decades 
        that infants can learn to read before they speak, absorb encyclopedic knowledge at 
        extraordinary rates, and develop enhanced memory capabilities — if information is 
        presented correctly.
      </p>
      <p>
        The problem: these methods require parents to manually create thousands of flashcards, 
        maintain complex rotation schedules, and deliver content at precise speeds. Most families 
        give up within weeks.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">The Vision</h2>
      <blockquote class="vision-quote">
        "What if AI could generate infinite, personalized educational content and deliver it 
        using the exact protocols that unlock a child's cognitive potential?"
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        <strong>tbt</strong> (tiny big thoughts) is a Cognitive Acceleration System that synthesizes:
      </p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>Doman's Bits of Intelligence</strong> — Precise, discrete, unambiguous images</li>
        <li><strong>Shichida's High-Speed Flashing</strong> — Sub-second (0.5s) presentation to engage right-brain processing</li>
        <li><strong>Artificial Synesthesia</strong> — Color-coded letters as additional memory retrieval cues</li>
        <li><strong>Generative AI</strong> — Unlimited, personalized content from LLMs and image models</li>
        <li><strong>Gaze Tracking</strong> — Attention-adaptive pacing and engagement analytics</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section demo-section">
      <h2 class="section-label">Working Prototype</h2>
      <div class="demo-embed">
        <iframe src="/prototypes/tbt/index.html" width="100%" height="600" frameborder="0"></iframe>
      </div>
      <p class="demo-caption">
        <a href="/prototypes/tbt/index.html" target="_blank" class="demo-link">Open full prototype →</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">Key Features</h2>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">⚡</span>
          <h3>Turbo Mode</h3>
          <p>0.5-second flashing bypasses analytical processing, depositing information directly into long-term memory.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">🎨</span>
          <h3>Synesthetic Text</h3>
          <p>Each letter has a consistent color based on common grapheme-color associations, creating additional neural pathways.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">📚</span>
          <h3>Encyclopedic Curriculum</h3>
          <p>Organized by taxonomy: Biology, Geography, Art, Music, Anatomy — building systematic knowledge.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-icon">🤖</span>
          <h3>AI Content Generation</h3>
          <p>GPT-4 + DALL-E + ElevenLabs voice cloning generate unlimited, fresh educational material.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">The Science</h2>
      <div class="science-grid">
        <div class="science-point">
          <h4>0–36 Months: The Critical Window</h4>
          <p>Explosive synaptogenesis creates neural connections at a rate never matched again. Use it or lose it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="science-point">
          <h4>Right-Brain Dominance</h4>
          <p>Infants process information holistically, not sequentially. Fast presentation aligns with their cognitive mode.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="science-point">
          <h4>Reading Before Speaking</h4>
          <p>Visual pathway development parallels auditory. Children can recognize written words before articulating them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="science-point">
          <h4>No Testing Rule</h4>
          <p>Doman forbids quizzing — it causes stress. Progress tracked via gaze patterns, not correct/incorrect.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">Technical Architecture</h2>
      <div class="tech-stack">
        <div class="tech-item">
          <strong>Frontend:</strong> FlutterFlow (native mobile for 0.5s flash rendering)
        </div>
        <div class="tech-item">
          <strong>Backend:</strong> Firebase + Knowledge Graph database
        </div>
        <div class="tech-item">
          <strong>AI Models:</strong> GPT-4o (curriculum), DALL-E 3 (images), ElevenLabs (voice cloning)
        </div>
        <div class="tech-item">
          <strong>Biofeedback:</strong> SeeSo SDK for gaze tracking and attention analytics
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">The Potential</h2>
      <p>
        If successful, tbt creates a generation of early readers with enhanced visualization 
        capabilities and encyclopedic knowledge bases. The Artificial Synesthesia component 
        alone represents a frontier experiment in cognitive scaffolding that could redefine 
        how literacy is taught globally.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>This isn't an educational app. It's a Cognitive Acceleration System.</strong>
      </p>
    </section>
    
    <section class="section related-section">
      <h2 class="section-label">Related</h2>
      <div class="related-links">
        <a href="/industries/education">Education Hub →</a>
        <a href="/ai">AI Tenet →</a>
        <a href="/case-studies/investing-dojo">Investing Dojo →</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .case-study {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
    padding-top: 0;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .case-header {
    padding: 8rem 0 4rem;
    text-align: center;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .case-meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .case-tenets, .case-industry {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .case-tenets a, .case-industry a {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .case-tenets a {
    background: #222;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .case-industry a {
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.2);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .case-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .case-tagline {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .vision-quote {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .feature-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .feature-list li {
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .feature-list li::before {
    content: "→";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .demo-section {
    background: #111;
    padding: 2rem;
    margin: 0 -2rem;
  }

  .demo-embed {
    background: #000;
    border: 1px solid #333;
  }

  .demo-embed iframe {
    display: block;
  }

  .demo-caption {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .demo-link {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .feature-card {
    background: #111;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid #333;
  }

  .feature-icon {
    font-size: 2rem;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .feature-card h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .feature-card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .science-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .science-point {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: #0a0a0a;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .science-point h4 {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .science-point p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .tech-stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .tech-item {
    padding: 1rem;
    background: #111;
    border: 1px solid #333;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .tech-item strong {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .related-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .related-links a {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .feature-grid,
    .science-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .demo-section {
      margin: 0 -1rem;
      padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
